Subject: [PATCH] feat(growth): attribution capture, connections UI, break a
 require cycle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the two gaps that made the growth stack incomplete rather than merely
unfinished.

1. ATTRIBUTION CAPTURE — the write side.
   growth_attribution_touchpoints had readers and no writer, so Attribution was
   guaranteed to be empty for every live tenant no matter how many providers
   were connected. Now:

   src/lib/growth/attribution.ts captures utm_*, gclid/fbclid/ttclid, referrer
   and landing path. First touch is kept in localStorage so a bride who finds
   you on Instagram in March and books in May is still credited to Instagram;
   the session id lives in sessionStorage so each visit is its own touch rather
   than collapsing weeks of browsing into one event. Storage access is wrapped
   because private-mode Safari throws, and tracking must never break a booking
   form. It no-ops in the demo plane — recording synthetic prospects against a
   real tenant would corrupt the owner's numbers.

   worker tracking.ts exposes POST /track and POST /track/identify. These are
   deliberately unauthenticated because the visitors they record are anonymous
   and always will be — the same trade every analytics pixel makes. The surface
   is kept small on purpose: append-only, business must resolve or 404, every
   field whitelisted and length-capped, per-IP rate limit, and 204 with no body
   so it can never be used as a read oracle. Verified: 400 on missing fields,
   404 on unknown business, 400 when identify has no id to link, while
   /sync/social still 401s without a token.

   deriveChannel() maps raw parameters to the SAME channel names the ad syncs
   write into growth_channel_spend. If those drifted, spend would land on one
   row and conversions on a lookalike, and every ROAS number would be quietly
   wrong while still looking plausible. 9 tests pin it, including that a
   self-referral is Direct rather than laundered into Referral.

2. CONNECTIONS UI — connecting no longer requires curl.
   GrowthConnectionsPanel lists every provider with live status, last sync time
   and last error, and offers Connect / Reconnect / Sync now. Each call carries
   the caller's access token; the worker still derives business_id from the
   membership, so the browser never names a tenant. OAuth uses a full navigation
   rather than a popup, because popups are blocked by default on mobile Safari,
   which is where a boutique owner usually is. Approval-gated providers say so
   inline instead of failing mysteriously later.

3. REQUIRE CYCLE — found by the new tests, not by review.
   store.ts and auth.ts imported productionSupabase from src/index.ts while
   index.ts imports the routers back. Production survived it only because
   index.ts is the entry point and resolves first; any other entry point got a
   partially-initialised module and died with "Router.use() requires a
   middleware function but got a undefined". The growth module now owns its
   service-role client (client.ts) and is a leaf that depends on env, not on the
   app that mounts it.

21 worker tests, 16/16 guard tests, 37 frontend unit tests, typecheck clean.

